ng to make that a  large majority their works cut out for  them given the fact that much of this is  very confusing it's very legal it's very  deep in the weeds and there's also this  challenge to that these are sort of the  Washington insiders that Donald Trump  campaigned against that he said he  wanted to drain the swamp that he these  are the people that control the power so  there are a number of narratives that  are sort of percolating underneath here  that are going to be a challenge for the  Democrats to put forward to make their  case yeah one of the things that we  heard a lot of from from both of these  witnesses was  the influence of rudy guiliani the  president's personal lawyer and his  involvement in all of this and the  perception that he was essentially  engaging in in a separate u.s. foreign  policy they talked about a regular  channel and an irregular Channel yeah it  wasn't just said once it was said  multiple times and this is the problem  for this White House that he the  ambassador Taylor used words like  alarmed that there were two channels it  was irregular it was crazy  essentially underscoring that there was  one channel for foreign policy with  respect to Ukraine that was the typical  diplomatic State Department Channel and  the other one that was operating under  the trump administration headed up by  the president's personal lawyer Rudolph  Giuliani  all right Kimberly for the moment thanks  very much Kimberly halket outside the  White House force let's go back to  Joseph or associate professor of  political science at Texas A&amp;M  University in the cutter joining us here  from Doha so I want to ask you then  about Rudy Giuliani what do you make of  the fact that you know he was he was  mentioned quite prominently in that  testimony the White House personal  lawyer and what what they saw as his  kind of unseemly involvement in the  whole u.s. relationship with Ukraine I  mean it's certainly not unusual for  presidents to use personal 